Hi Taro

On Friday 25 November 2011 10:02:16 Taro Yamazaki wrote:
> Here is the Japanized .rc file.
> Please import it to the source repository.

Thanks for your contribution, very much appreciated. I've already built a=20
version of the GUI to find out what Japanese will look like.

One thing I'd like to ask is if you could send the .rc file again in UTF-8=
=20
encoding. I'm having trouble decoding it from SJJS. I'm getting several=20
warnings about unrecognized escape sequences and as I plan to switch to UTF=
-8=20
encoded language files anyways, that will probably solve the problem.

One thing I noticed is that you changed the dialog font name to "=EF=BC=AD=
=EF=BC=B3 =EF=BC=B0=E3=82=B4=E3=82=B7=E3=83=83=E3=82=AF". Is=20
"Microsoft Sans Serif" installed on Japanese Windows? Using "=EF=BC=AD=EF=
=BC=B3 =EF=BC=B0=E3=82=B4=E3=82=B7=E3=83=83=E3=82=AF" on an=20
English Windows XP (with Eastern Asian language support installed) makes th=
e=20
dialogs and controls within appear smaller (check the attached image). Usin=
g=20
"Microsoft Sans Serif" still displays the katakana correctly while preservi=
ng=20
the original size. So, if that doesn't cause any problems on your side I'll=
=20
use "Microsoft Sans Serif" instead.

